ow much do you feed it if you're not going to bake? So confusing!","thread":{"-NwvhqGyg9FN5zgc1qHZ":{"author":"Melisa Smith","notifications":true,"page":"http:\/\/www.theglasspantry.com\/care-and-keeping-sourdough-starter","pageTitle":"Care and Keeping of Sourdough Starter","path":"\/care-and-keeping-sourdough-starter","text":"Hi Donna. After feeding your starter a few times it will become much greater in volume. I usually discard or make something using the \"discard\" after 2 feedings. Some people like to discard before each feeding but if you are trying to bulk up your starter for baking you will need the volume so I like to discard less often. Feel free to stop feeding it and put it in the fridge if your not going to be baking with it. It will keep for a long time (weeks) like that. After removing it from the refrigerator, feed it equal parts flour and water once or twice and let it stay at room temperature until you see the bubbling activity before using it for baking. Hope that helps. Let me know if you have any questions. Happy Baking!","time":1714693825741,"userId":"9acc1803bb49d8e1f565ad16cecad0ab","userType":"email"}},"time":1714690257492,"userId":"de427ec6271ec531dac89fe6905f58f3","userType":"email"}},"texts":null};
